# General Project Rules

## Code Style & Structure
- Use TypeScript for all development with strict type checking enabled.
- Follow consistent naming conventions: PascalCase for components/types, camelCase for variables/functions.
- Keep files under 300 lines of code when possible.
- Split complex logic into smaller, reusable functions.
- Use meaningful comments for complex logic, but prefer self-documenting code.
- Always use proper indentation (2 spaces) and consistent formatting.

## Performance
- Minimize unnecessary re-renders with proper hooks usage and memoization.
- Implement code-splitting and lazy loading for large components/pages.
- Optimize bundle size by avoiding unnecessary dependencies.
- Use server components where possible to reduce client-side JavaScript.

## Project Structure
- Maintain a clear and organized folder structure with separation of concerns:
  ```
  /app
    /(routes)                # Route groups with pages
      /(auth)                # Auth-protected routes
      /(public)              # Public routes
      /[entity]/             # Entity-specific routes
        page.tsx             # Server component (page entry)
        [id]/                # Dynamic route (detail pages)
        _components/         # Page-specific components
    /api                     # API routes
    /auth                    # Auth-related components

  /components
    /ui                      # Shared UI components
    /layout                  # Layout components
    /forms                   # Form components

  /lib
    /query                   # Query client setup
    /services                # Service layer for data fetching
    /supabase                # Supabase client setup
      /schema                # Supabase table definitions and SQL queries
    /storage                 # File and data storage utilities
    /utils                   # Utility functions

  /hooks                     # Custom React hooks
  /types                     # TypeScript types
  /styles                    # Global styles
  /public                    # Static assets
  ```

## Error Handling
- Implement proper error boundaries at appropriate levels.
- Use consistent error handling patterns across the application.
- Always handle promise rejections and catch exceptions.
- Provide user-friendly error messages while logging detailed errors for debugging.

## Accessibility & Internationalization
- Ensure components are accessible (use proper ARIA attributes).
- Support dark mode with appropriate color contrasts.
- Use semantic HTML elements wherever possible.
- Implement internationalization for text content when required.

## Version Control
- Write clear, descriptive commit messages.
- Create meaningful pull request descriptions.
- Keep pull requests focused on a single feature or fix.

## Development Workflow
- Always write tests for critical functionality.
- Use feature flags for new features when appropriate.
- Document complex implementations and architectural decisions.